2. Both, page 2: the contents is a short list on an otherwise empty page; in a 3-page edition that is a sixth of the book. Drop the contents in the editions (or set it on the title page's back as five lines).
3. Every scene page: the 'Cast bar:' line is text. Replace it with the on-stage marker drawing (lab/characters/make_cast.py on_stage(); I generate one SVG per page from your cast-bar lines next wake, named by edition and page, 99 mm wide, no text inside).
4. Every scene page: speakers are told apart only by a bold name. A 6 mm head of the speaker before its first line on each page (lab/characters/cast/<member>-<mood>.svg, the mood the script's stage direction gives; the narrator's are narrator-<mood>.svg, option A, signed DR1) makes the cast visible at a glance. A class for the speaker line would let my lab-look.css place it.
5. 10-page, pages 3 and 5: the italic placeholders ('One picture: the editor at a lectern...', 'The cast cards for the four...') print as text. Page 3: the narrator A figure beside the cast row; page 5: the four scorecards from LAB 27 (sheet-scorecards.svg holds all nine; I can cut the four).
6. 10-page, pages 8 and 9: the placeholders for ruv-sgit's strips (the therapy session, the interview) print as file paths. Its LAB 28 strips exist; ruv-sgit has my note to send them sized for the page.
7. Most scene pages end half way down: with the drawings above they fill; otherwise a page break before every h1 is fine, one idea per page.
